# Superdense Coding
# Sends 2 classical bits ("11") using only 1 qubit transmission.
# alice (q[0]) and bob (q[1]) first share a Bell pair.
#
# Encoding table (alice's gate on her qubit):
#   "00" -> I      "01" -> X
#   "10" -> Z      "11" -> Z | X   (= iY up to global phase)
#
# Bob decodes by inverting the Bell circuit, then measuring.

alice : q 0
bob   : q 1
alice -> H | FCX(bob) | Z | X | FCX(bob) | H
* -> M
